WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:03.436
I'm, uh -- I'm doing better.

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:06.139
[ Laughter ]

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:09.642
I -- I just turned 39,
you know, which is --

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.110
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.878
Okay. Yeah, yeah.
Yeah, it's not old.

00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:14.948
It's not -- It's not old.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:20.887
But I think we can all agree
that I am running out of time.

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:22.422
Sure. Yeah.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:27.593
I got about one year left
on this fun little outfit.

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:29.896
And then I got to regroup.

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.898
I've got to become
a businessman next year.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:34.066
I've got to start talking
like a 40-year-old.

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:36.202
I've got start staying
40-year-old words.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.470
Like, "Terrific.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:40.907
"This is bull."

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:42.976
"Absolute bull."

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.910
"This is a lease."

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.946
"You're not on the lease!"

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:50.449
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.449 --> 00:00:52.652
All of a sudden gonna wake up
with a 14-year-old son

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.654
named Michael.

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:57.123
"Get your head out of your butt,
Michael!

00:00:57.123 --> 00:01:00.326
Quit loafing around
and get a job!

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.462
You're up there
playing your vidya games!"

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:04.163
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:07.400
When I was 14, my dad hated
I did not have a job.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.569
He was always like,
"Quit loafing around!

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.604
Get a job!"

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:14.474
I was like, "I'm 14!
I think it's illegal."

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:16.542
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:18.511
He's like, "You're going to
print off some résumés."

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.513
I was like,
"Print off some résumés?

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.949
What am I gonna put on the
résumé? I've never had a job.

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:24.150
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:26.152
I kid you not,
he made me print off résumés,

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.421
and all they said on them was,

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:31.190
"Raked Judith Hoye's leaves."

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.826
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:39.098
I walked into businesses.
I was like, "Here's my CV.

00:01:39.098 --> 00:01:40.934
Give Judith Hoye a ring."

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.002
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.503 --> 00:01:48.908
I got fired from
a lot of jobs growing up.

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:51.110
One job I got fired from
when I was a teenager --

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:53.879
this is 100% true --
is I was a house painter.

00:01:53.879 --> 00:01:57.550
I used to paint the outside
of people's homes.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:01.688
And how I got fired from
that job is, long story short,

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:03.088
um...

00:02:03.088 --> 00:02:04.891
I painted the wrong house.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.225
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:08.327
Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:08.327 --> 00:02:10.130
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:14.533
Yeah, so, painted
the wrong house,

00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:17.737
and then I guess
what happened was,

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:20.206
is the people who live there,

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:23.075
they left for work
early in the morning,

00:02:23.075 --> 00:02:27.013
you know, stupidly assuming
no one's gonna paint their home.

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:28.314
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.149
Yeah.

00:02:30.149 --> 00:02:34.353
Yeah, and then we pulled in the
driveway like one second later

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:37.123
and committed a crime
for eight hours.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.824
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.824 --> 00:02:41.494
Yeah. In the sun.

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:44.763
And then our boss finally
figured out where we were.

00:02:44.763 --> 00:02:47.367
He was like, "Oh, my God!
You painted the wrong house!"

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.769
And this is --
And then -- You know.

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:51.303
And this is how
we solved the problem.

00:02:51.303 --> 00:02:53.105
Now, pay close attention.

00:02:53.105 --> 00:02:55.274
We packed everything up
and drove away.

00:02:55.274 --> 00:02:56.609
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:58.410
Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:00.579
And then we were fired
on the way home.

00:03:00.579 --> 00:03:02.381
That makes sense. We're morons.

00:03:02.381 --> 00:03:04.350
But what that means, though,
is I never got to find out

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:10.056
what happened to that family
when they got home from work

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:13.126
and their house
was a different color!

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:15.662
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:19.532
And nobody had any answers.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:23.670
When they started their day,

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:27.307
they owned a white house
with gray trim.

00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:32.445
And when they finished their
day, their house was brown.

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:34.814
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:38.217
Brown!

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:40.219
Now, sometimes people ask me --

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:42.922
They go,
"But what shade of brown?"

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.490
And I'm like -- I don't know.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.326
I like to describe it
as a noticeable brown.

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:49.495
Uh, yeah, the kind of brown
you're going to notice

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.630
your house is a completely
different color

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:53.365
than when
you started your day --

00:03:53.365 --> 00:03:55.501
and wet.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.570
Now, I don't know what
that couple said to each other

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.705
when they got home.
I have no idea.

00:03:59.705 --> 00:04:03.442
But I'm pretty sure
they did not say a single word.

00:04:03.442 --> 00:04:07.479
Because how do you ask
your spouse

00:04:07.479 --> 00:04:10.049
if your house was always brown?

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:11.517
I don't know.

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.886
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you very much.

